The code was written for SigmaM2M, a oneM2M platform, from public
descriptions of the WiZ local API (PROVENANCE.md). It contains no code
from other projects. sim/sim.go comes from SigmaM2M and carries no
per-file copyright header, the convention of the code it comes from; the
copyright line above covers it. Files added for this module carry
"Copyright 2026 Abhinav Gautam" and "SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0".

WiZ is a trademark of its owner. This module is not made, endorsed or
supported by the owner of the WiZ products; the name is used only to say
which devices it simulates.

Facts from other projects
-------------------------

The vendor does not publish the local API. The method names, parameter
names, ports, module names and scene numbers the simulator uses are
facts read from public descriptions, chiefly pywizlight
(github.com/sbidy/pywizlight; MIT, Copyright (c) 2020 Stephan Traub).
No code was taken; see PROVENANCE.md.

Dependencies
------------

- The Go standard library (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright The Go Authors).
- github.com/cB-Sigma/wiz (the WiZ local API client; Copyright 2026
  Abhinav Gautam, Apache-2.0). Used by the tests and the command.
- github.com/cB-Sigma/lanbcast (indirect, through wiz; LAN broadcast
  helper; Copyright 2026 Abhinav Gautam, Apache-2.0, standard library
  only).

Test data
---------

Every MAC address, module name, firmware version, power reading and
address in the simulator, the tests and cmd/wizsim is a made-up demo
value.
